WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:04.381
- [Onnia Harris] We had nothing;

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:06.731
it was just condemned land.

00:00:06.731 --> 00:00:08.701
You've got something that's dead and ugly

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:09.923
and you just make it beautiful

00:00:09.923 --> 00:00:12.108
and that's what they did.

00:00:12.108 --> 00:00:15.691
(railroad crossing chimes)

00:00:17.378 --> 00:00:18.859
- I think the farthest away I am

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:21.606
from any of the relatives
is seven minutes.

00:00:21.606 --> 00:00:22.439
- Hey, Grandma.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.248
(laughs)

00:00:24.248 --> 00:00:25.081
- And I like that.

00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:26.972
I just like the area.

00:00:26.972 --> 00:00:28.798
- It's nice to have the family around

00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:30.097
because we right here,

00:00:30.097 --> 00:00:32.408
so that's like the best thing.

00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:34.987
Pullman, everybody know
as far as the 1800s,

00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:37.357
it's known for its railroad cars.

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:40.078
It used to look like a
raggedly neighborhood to me.

00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:41.187
- [Grandma] Bye, kids.

00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:44.354
- It was hard to get a job in Pullman.

00:00:46.034 --> 00:00:48.166
A lot of times by me
being a single parent,

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:50.929
it's hard for mothers to
always be away from they kids.

00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:53.728
I used to spend like two
hours just traveling,

00:00:53.728 --> 00:00:55.947
trying to get to my job,

00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:58.709
but now I've got a job right
in my own neighborhood,

00:00:58.709 --> 00:00:59.610
which is great.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.741
Has anyone been to the factory

00:01:00.741 --> 00:01:03.786
with all the pretty colors
on the building down 111th?

00:01:03.786 --> 00:01:05.306
It's not your normal warehouse.

00:01:05.306 --> 00:01:06.547
I'm the one that's responsible

00:01:06.547 --> 00:01:09.768
for printing this fine print
on our bottles for Method.

00:01:09.768 --> 00:01:11.645
The company is about being yourself

00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:13.745
and having fun while you're at work.

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:14.594
Hey, Tony.

00:01:14.594 --> 00:01:16.933
Method, they've been here
almost three years now.

00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:18.834
For them to come choose this location

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.308
was like a blessing to everybody.

00:01:21.308 --> 00:01:22.202
I came in with no skills

00:01:22.202 --> 00:01:24.312
and they taught me everything
that I need to know.

00:01:24.312 --> 00:01:25.145
Hey, Jimmy.

00:01:25.145 --> 00:01:26.130
(laughs)

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.850
We really come in and help this community.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:28.736
You know, we bring in people

00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:30.448
that's from this area code,

00:01:30.448 --> 00:01:31.281
giving them a job,

00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:32.368
and we're gonna teach them.

00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:33.408
Like, we're not gonna just say,

00:01:33.408 --> 00:01:35.709
you're not good enough.

00:01:35.709 --> 00:01:38.046
It's a messy job, but
I finally got it clean.

00:01:38.046 --> 00:01:40.320
(laughs)

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.818
I come in starting off at packing bottles

00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:44.722
to running the soap screen.

00:01:44.722 --> 00:01:46.881
As long as it's running great, perfect,

00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:49.442
but there's some times
where we missing a line here

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.584
or the barcode's bad,

00:01:50.584 --> 00:01:53.042
that's when I gotta get in with my tools.

00:01:53.042 --> 00:01:55.042
Working at that machine
got me feeling handy.

00:01:55.042 --> 00:01:57.301
Now I feel like SuperWoman,
all I need is my cape;

00:01:57.301 --> 00:01:58.134
that's it.

00:01:58.134 --> 00:01:59.389
(laughs)

00:01:59.389 --> 00:02:01.722
(pop music)

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.069
Everybody say you have
kids at a young age,

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:06.117
you become a statistic,

00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:10.320
but they became like
my biggest motivation.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.835
It's just bigger than just,

00:02:11.835 --> 00:02:14.240
oh, we're making soap or I just got a job,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.122
they know that Mom working for us.

00:02:17.122 --> 00:02:20.031
A lot of people they don't
see all the bigger picture.

00:02:20.031 --> 00:02:21.002
My whole family here,

00:02:21.002 --> 00:02:22.082
I didn't wanna just leave them

00:02:22.082 --> 00:02:24.412
so if I can stay and make a difference

00:02:24.412 --> 00:02:25.813
and an impact on the community,

00:02:25.813 --> 00:02:27.562
make it better in my own neighborhood.

00:02:27.562 --> 00:02:28.870
It not serve purpose just for me,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.787
it'll serve for my family as well.

